# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gitCheck — Environment Variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub API
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A classic GitHub Personal Access Token with NO scopes needed for public repos.
# Raises the API rate limit from 60 requests/hour (unauthenticated) to
# 5,000 requests/hour — essential for scanning repos without hitting limits.
#
# Create one at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   1. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
#   2. Name it: gitcheck-local
#   3. Expiration: 90 days (or your preference)
#   4. Leave EVERY scope unchecked — public repos need nothing
#   5. Click "Generate" and copy the value (starts with `ghp_`)
#
# Format: ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Required: Yes
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site URL (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public URL of the deployed site. Used for generating Open Graph image
# URLs and share links. Falls back to the production URL if not set.
#
# In production (Vercel), this is set in the dashboard.
# For local development, leave it as http://localhost:3000.
#
# Format: https://your-domain.com
# Required: No (defaults to https://gitcheck-two.vercel.app)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000